       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8000 mg per dose is more than double the total daily maximum of 3,200 mg, and the order would deliver 32,000 mg/day. No indication supports that dose, and it would likely cause serious harm in a 70 kg patient.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a few ways:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose such as 400 or 600 mg.\n- **Check the intent.** If you meant a different drug, a different unit, or a different dose, tell me and I'll enter that.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for a nonstandard dose, a pharmacist or clinical pharmacology consult can review it. They can also enter it through a channel with the right safeguards.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
